# ---- Lanyard (Discord presence) — powers two hero widgets ----
#   * "Now Playing" (bottom-left)          — your live Spotify track
#   * "Watching on YouTube" (bottom-right) — a "Watching YouTube" Rich Presence,
#     i.e. the PreMiD browser extension with its YouTube presence enabled
# Setup:
#   1. Join the Lanyard Discord:  https://discord.gg/lanyard
#   2. Discord -> Settings -> Connections -> connect Spotify
#      (for the YouTube card: install PreMiD + its YouTube presence, keep Discord running)
#   3. Discord -> Settings -> Advanced -> Developer Mode on,
#      right-click your username -> Copy User ID
#   4. Copy this file to .env.local, paste the id, restart `npm run dev`.
VITE_LANYARD_ID=1489321223497191425

# ---- YouTube "Last Watched" fallback (bottom-right card) ----
# YouTube has no watch-history API, so when you're not actively watching, the
# card shows the most-recently-added video from a public playlist you curate.
#   1. Make a PUBLIC (or unlisted) playlist, e.g. "Recently Watched", and add
#      videos to it as you watch. Copy its id from the URL: ...?list=PLxxxxxxxx
#   2. Reuse the YouTube Data API v3 key from the steps you already did
#      (console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services; key restricted to
#      YouTube Data API v3 + Websites vineethsagar.co.in/* , *.vineethsagar.co.in/* , localhost:5173/*)
# Blank -> the card just shows the live presence / cache / "Offline".
VITE_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
VITE_YOUTUBE_WATCHED_PLAYLIST_ID=
